## GitHub Actions

The workflow in `.github/workflows/robot.yml` uses the same profiles as locally:

| Job | Command | When |
|-----|---------|------|
| `check` | Robocop and `robotcode -p ci -p check robot` | on every push and pull request |
| `test` | `robotcode -p ci -p dev robot` | after `check`; started by hand with a selectable environment |
| `template-check` | compares the project with the branch `rf-{{ rf_version }}` of the template | on the default branch; warning (hint only) when there is something new - see [Updating from the template](#updating-from-the-template) |

Against another environment: choose `test` or `prod` under *Actions > Robot Framework > Run workflow*. The
results (`results/`) are attached to the run as artifact `results`. Store the private CryptoLibrary key as a
*repository secret*.
