## Updating from the template

This project was generated from a template. **Where** it comes from is stored in `.copier-answers.yml`:
`_src_path` is the address of the template, `_commit` the version the project was created or last updated
from. Improvements of the template do **not** arrive automatically - you pull them yourself.

The template has one version per Robot Framework version (branch `rf-<version>`). This project uses Robot
Framework **{{ rf_version }}**. Always pass `--vcs-ref` when updating - without it, Copier takes the newest
template version and raises the Robot Framework version, too:

```bash
git status                                                  # everything committed? copier update needs a clean state
uvx copier update --trust --vcs-ref rf-{{ rf_version }}     # take over improvements, version stays {{ rf_version }}
git diff                                                    # look at the changes
uv sync                                                     # install packages matching the new pyproject.toml
uv run robotcode robot                                      # test, then commit
```

Copier only applies the **differences** between the old and the new template version. Your own tests and
keywords are kept. Where you and the template changed the same place, you get a conflict like in Git
(markers `<<<<<<<` / `>>>>>>>` in the file) - resolve it, then commit. If the address of the template changed,
adjust the line `_src_path` in `.copier-answers.yml`.

### Newer versions of the libraries

Apart from Robot Framework, the libraries have no fixed version; `uv.lock` holds the state the project was
set up with. This is how you see what is new and take it over:

```bash
uv tree --outdated --depth 1     # shows the newest available version per library
uv lock --upgrade                # move to the newest matching versions
uv sync                          # install
uv run robotcode robot           # test, then commit
```

You move to a newer Robot Framework version on purpose with the branch of that version, e.g.
`uvx copier update --trust --vcs-ref rf-<new-version>`. The available versions are listed in the template's
documentation (`docs/versions-and-updates.md`).
